# The knowledge base commits only the *system* (manifest, updater, our notes) and
# non-reproducible vendored assets. All fetched content is regenerated by update.py
# (`uv run --with pyyaml python update.py`) so it stays out of git — keeps the repo
# lean and avoids committing stale snapshots of docs that change upstream.

# --- fetched PDFs (reproducible via sources.yaml) ---
ableton/live_manual/*.pdf
hardware/novation_launchpad_x/*.pdf
hardware/jomox_alphabase/*.pdf

# --- cloned decompiled script repos (each has its own .git) ---
ableton/scripting/midi_remote_scripts/*/

# --- website mirrors ---
ableton/scripting/midi_remote_api/structure_void_mirror/
ableton/max_for_live/mirror/

# --- crawl logs ---
_mirror_logs/

# NOTE: hardware/faderfox/** is intentionally NOT ignored — those manuals/firmware/
# templates are vendored (no upstream source URL) and must be committed.
# ableton/scripting/extensions_sdk/ is NOT ignored — its docs are gated and must be
# committed by hand once downloaded (not reproducible by update.py).
plugins/*/*.pdf
plugins/*/*.txt
